// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Suspicious Explorer Process with Whitespace Padding - ClickFix/FileFix
// Sigma ID: 74a7aea5-0076-4f4a-b2ba-c9e26adbaca5
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-11-04 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1204.004, T1027.010
// Description: Detects process creation with suspicious whitespace padding followed by a '#' character, which
//   may indicate ClickFix or FileFix techniques used to conceal malicious commands from visual
//   inspection. ClickFix and FileFix are social engineering attack techniques where adversaries
//   distribute phishing documents or malicious links that deceive users into opening the Windows Run
//   dialog box or File Explorer search bar. The victims are then instructed to paste commands from
//   their clipboard, which contain extensive whitespace padding using various Unicode space
//   characters to push the actual malicious command far to the right, effectively hiding it from
//   immediate view.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://expel.com/blog/cache-smuggling-when-a-picture-isnt-a-thousand-words/
//   - https://mrd0x.com/filefix-clickfix-alternative/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ebd26c2d9cd57dc9489faa1f1346577be9947747/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_clickfix_filefix_whitespace_padding.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "#") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            " or ProcessCommandLine contains "            ")
